{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"e0f1673e856ee8fb61b039fdb3782fe9c6a20488741b403968ed0134b3fb1943","packTokens":6394,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":6313,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that is not paid or closed and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response is 200 and contains INV-1\",\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due) when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response does not contain INV-2\",\n    \"Given business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response contains INV-3\",\n    \"Given the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10 and today is 2026-10-15 when the overdue list is requested then an open invoice due 2026-10-05 is included and an open invoice due 2026-10-06 is not\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice has a paid or closed status in the existing invoice data, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list whatever its due date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoice C is 30 days past its due date with status paid and invoice D is 30 days past its due date with status closed when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then neither C nor D is in the response\",\n    \"Given invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data when the overdue list is requested again then INV-6 is no longer in the response, with no other action needed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders API shall work out overdue status when it is queried and shall not write any overdue flag or status to invoice records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue when the overdue list endpoint and the invoice detail endpoint for an overdue invoice are called then every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return, for each overdue invoice, its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given today is 2026-10-15 in the business timezone and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, is due 2026-10-01 when the overdue list is requested then the INV-100 entry has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 14\",\n    \"Given today is 2026-09-08 and open invoice INV-1 is due 2026-09-01 with threshold 7 when the overdue list is requested then the INV-1 entry has days overdue 7\",\n    \"Given 3 overdue invoices and 2 invoices that are not overdue when an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint then the response contains exactly the 3 overdue invoices\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given customer A has 2 overdue invoices and customer B has 3 overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer A then the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices\",\n    \"Given customer C has no overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C then the response is 200 with an empty list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or 91 and over (90+), the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue falls inside that bucket, bounds included.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91 when the overdue list is requested with each bucket in turn then 7–30 returns 7 and 30; 31–60 returns 31 and 60; 61–90 returns 61 and 90; 90+ returns only 91\",\n    \"Given customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days and customer B has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days when the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60 then only customer A's 40-day invoice is returned\",\n    \"Given any data when the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets (e.g. 5-9) then the response is 400 and names the allowed bucket values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to the overdue list, invoice detail or send-reminder endpoint has no valid staff authentication under the existing API's authentication scheme, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401, return no invoice or customer data, and send no email.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no authentication credentials when the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are each called then each response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body, the email provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\",\n    \"Given an expired or invalid staff token and an overdue invoice when the overdue list endpoint and the send-reminder endpoint for that invoice are called then both responses are 401 and the email provider stub receives no call\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has an email address, the invoice reminders API shall send one email through the configured transactional email provider to the single email address on the customer record, using the configured template and containing the invoice number, amount and due date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-100 (amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01) belongs to a customer with email accounts@crumb.example, and a stubbed email provider when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 2xx and the provider stub receives exactly one send request addressed to accounts@crumb.example whose body contains 'INV-100', '250.00' and '2026-10-01'\",\n    \"Given the template in configuration is changed to a different subject line when a reminder is sent then the provider stub receives the new subject line\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the customer record of the invoice has no email address, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the send-reminder request with HTTP 422 and an error saying the customer has no email address, shall not call the email provider, and shall not record a reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-200 belongs to a customer whose email field is empty when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-200 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 422 with a message saying the customer has no email address, the provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request is for an invoice that is not currently overdue, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the request with HTTP 409 and an error saying the invoice is not overdue, and shall not call the email provider.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoice INV-21 has status paid when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-21 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 409 saying the invoice is not overdue, and the email provider stub receives no request\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a reminder send is attempted with the email provider, the invoice reminders API shall store a reminder history entry holding the invoice, the authenticated staff user who sent it, the UTC timestamp of the attempt, and a delivery status of sent or failed with a failure reason when failed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given staff user 'sam' is authenticated, INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email, and the provider stub accepts the send when sam sends a reminder for INV-100 at 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z then a reminder history row exists for INV-100 with sender 'sam', timestamp 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z (±5 s), status 'sent' and an empty failure reason\",\n    \"Given two reminders were sent for INV-100 more than 60 seconds apart by 'maria' and then 'tom' when the reminder history for INV-100 is read then two separate entries exist with senders 'maria' and 'tom' and their own timestamps\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the email provider returns an error or does not respond within the send timeout when a reminder is sent, then the invoice reminders API shall record the attempt as failed with the provider's reason, return an error response containing that reason, and keep the invoice on the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-100 and a provider stub that rejects the send with 'invalid recipient' when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 502 including 'invalid recipient', a reminder history row for INV-100 has status 'failed' and reason 'invalid recipient', and the overdue list still contains INV-100\",\n    \"Given a provider stub that does not respond within the configured send timeout when a reminder is sent for INV-100 then the attempt is recorded as 'failed' with a reason that says it timed out and an error response is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the email provider reports a bounce for a reminder previously recorded as sent, the invoice reminders API shall change that reminder history entry's status to failed and store the bounce reason, keeping the invoice on the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a reminder history entry for INV-100 has status 'sent' and provider message id 'msg-1' when the provider webhook endpoint receives a correctly signed bounce event for 'msg-1' with reason 'mailbox does not exist' then the response is 2xx, the entry has status 'failed' and reason 'mailbox does not exist', and INV-100 is still on the overdue list\",\n    \"Given no reminder history entry has provider message id 'msg-unknown' when a correctly signed bounce event for 'msg-unknown' is received then the response is 2xx and no reminder history row changes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a bounce webhook request fails the email provider's signature verification against the configured secret, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and change no reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a reminder history entry recorded as 'sent' with provider message id 'msg-1' when the webhook endpoint receives a bounce event for 'msg-1' whose signature is missing or invalid then the response is 401 and the entry still has status 'sent'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request for an invoice arrives within 60 seconds of an earlier accepted send-reminder request for the same invoice, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 409 as a duplicate, shall not call the email provider, and shall not record another reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email when two send-reminder requests for INV-100 are sent 1 second apart then the first returns 2xx, the second returns 409, the provider stub receives exactly one send request, and exactly one reminder history row exists for INV-100\",\n    \"Given a reminder for INV-100 was accepted at 09:00:00 when another send-reminder request for INV-100 arrives at 09:01:01 then the request succeeds, a second email is sent and a second history row is recorded\",\n    \"Given a reminder for INV-100 was accepted 10 seconds ago when a send-reminder request for a different overdue invoice INV-101 is made then the INV-101 request succeeds and an email is sent\",\n    \"Given two send-reminder requests for INV-100 sent at the same moment when both are processed then exactly one reaches the provider and the other returns 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's detail, the invoice reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer, amount, due date, whether it is overdue, and its full reminder history newest first, where each entry shows the sender, timestamp, delivery status and failure reason if there is one.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-100 with amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01, one 'sent' attempt by jo at 2026-10-08T09:00Z and one 'failed' attempt by sam at 2026-10-09T10:00Z with reason 'invalid recipient' when the invoice detail endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response has invoice number, customer, amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01, the overdue indicator, and history [sam 2026-10-09T10:00Z failed 'invalid recipient', jo 2026-10-08T09:00Z sent with no reason] in that order\",\n    \"Given an invoice with no reminders when its detail is requested then the response has an empty reminder history\",\n    \"Given invoice id 'does-not-exist' when the invoice detail endpoint is called for it then the response is 404\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The overdue list screen shall show the overdue invoices in a table with invoice number, customer, amount, due date and days overdue, a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, and a 'Send reminder' button on each row that stays disabled while its request is in progress and shows the success or failure result (with reason) when it ends.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a signed-in staff user and 3 overdue invoices for 2 customers when the user opens the overdue list screen, picks one customer in the customer filter and then the 7–30 bucket then the table shows only that customer's invoices in that bucket, with all five columns and a 'Send reminder' button on each row\",\n    \"Given the email provider stub is set to delay 3 seconds and then fail with 'invalid recipient' when the user clicks 'Send reminder' on a row and clicks it again straight away then the button is disabled until the request ends, only one request reaches the API, and the row then shows a failure message containing 'invalid recipient' while the invoice stays in the table\",\n    \"Given the overdue list screen is open and the provider stub accepts sends when the user clicks 'Send reminder' on a row then a success message is shown for that row once the response arrives\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's amount, due date, and reminder history with each attempt's sender, time and delivery status, with each delivery failure and its reason marked out, and a 'Send reminder' button for an overdue invoice.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-1 is overdue and has one sent and one failed ('mailbox full') reminder attempt when a signed-in staff user opens the INV-1 detail screen then amount and due date are shown, both history entries are listed newest first with sender, time and status, the failed entry shows 'mailbox full', and a 'Send reminder' button is shown\",\n    \"Given the invoice detail screen for an overdue invoice when the user clicks 'Send reminder' then a new history entry appears with the user's name, the current time and its delivery status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While the invoice is not overdue, the invoice detail screen shall not show the 'Send reminder' button.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-5 is paid when a signed-in staff user opens the INV-5 detail screen then no 'Send reminder' button is shown\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice detail screen shall show a 'Send reminder' button for any invoice it displays, whether or not the invoice is currently overdue.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-5 is paid when a signed-in staff user opens the INV-5 detail screen then a 'Send reminder' button is shown\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing).\",\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing).\",\n  \"The send-reminder endpoint gives the staff user a result within a fixed time, including when the provider is slow (d1 reading).\",\n  \"The send-reminder endpoint does not hang on a slow email provider (d2 reading).\",\n  \"Send-reminder endpoint response time including the provider call (d3 reading).\",\n  \"Bounce reports from the provider show up in reminder history soon after they arrive.\",\n  \"Customer email addresses (PII) are not written to application logs.\",\n  \"Every reminder attempt is kept for audit.\",\n  \"No duplicate emails come from double submits.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}